+# Product Requirements Document (PRD)
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Version**: 1.0.0  
+**Date**: 2026-08-11  
+**Status**: Planning  
+**Scale**: Level 2
+
+---
+
+## Information Sources
+
+**Traceability**: This plan uses only the supplied foundation:
+
+- `project.md` — vision, pilot outcome, and non-goals.
+- `context.md` — two engineers, four-week pilot, Python API, browser UI, and
+  an unselected reminder provider.
+- `product-contract.md` — PRM-001 through PRM-004.
+- `evidence-contract.md` — required end-to-end, tenant-isolation, and
+  facilitator-LARP evidence.
+- `architecture.md` — pilot modular-monolith and provider-adapter decisions.
+
+No research reports, UX strategy, design system, constitution, or brownfield
+artifacts were supplied; no external research was used.
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+Pulseboard turns an uploaded meeting transcript into proposed action items that
+a facilitator reviews. The product never schedules or sends an item until that
+facilitator has explicitly confirmed its text, owner, and due date. The pilot
+will serve five teams and aims for 80% proposal review with 30% fewer unowned,
+overdue actions in four weeks.
+
+## Product Vision & Strategy
+
+### Vision Statement
+
+Make the action-item follow-through after a meeting visible and trustworthy:
+automation helps surface likely work, while the facilitator retains the final
+decision before any reminder is delivered.
+
+### Strategic Objectives
+
+1. **Turn transcripts into reviewable proposals**: reduce the manual work of
+   finding action items without treating an extraction as a decision.
+2. **Make ownership explicit**: require a named owner and due date before an
+   action can move into delivery.
+3. **Earn pilot trust through control and isolation**: preserve facilitator
+   agency, show delivery state, and prevent cross-workspace access.
+
+### Success Definition
+
+- **Pilot success**: five teams use the workflow during a four-week pilot.
+- **User success**: 80% of proposed actions are reviewed by a facilitator.
+- **Outcome success**: teams have 30% fewer unowned overdue actions versus the
+  agreed pilot baseline.
+- **Trust success**: no action is delivered without an explicit complete
+  confirmation, and cross-workspace negative probes are denied.
+
+## Market Analysis
+
+### Target Market
+
+The supplied scope identifies meeting facilitators in pilot teams, not a
+market-size claim. TAM, SAM, and SOM are intentionally not estimated without
+evidence.
+
+### Competitive Landscape
+
+No competitor evidence was supplied. Pulseboard's planned differentiation is
+the review-before-delivery invariant, not autonomous outbound messaging.
+
+### Market Opportunity
+
+The immediate opportunity is a constrained pilot: validate whether reviewed
+action proposals reduce unowned overdue work before expanding the product.
+
+## User Analysis
+
+### User Personas
+
+**Meeting facilitator**
+
+- **Role**: uploads the transcript and is accountable for reviewing actions.
+- **Goals**: turn a meeting into clear commitments without manually rebuilding
+  a task list.
+- **Pain points**: proposed actions can be inaccurate, incomplete, or lack an
+  owner/due date.
+- **Success looks like**: every delivered reminder corresponds to an item the
+  facilitator knowingly confirmed.
+
+**Action owner**
+
+- **Role**: the person named on a confirmed action.
+- **Goals**: receive a clear reminder of a real commitment.
+- **Pain points**: vague, duplicated, or incorrectly assigned follow-up.
+- **Success looks like**: one understandable reminder with an accurate due
+  date and visible delivery state for the facilitator.
+
+### User Journey Map: Transcript to Follow-Through
+
+1. **Need**: a facilitator finishes a meeting and needs follow-up captured.
+2. **Upload**: the facilitator uploads a transcript to the correct workspace.
+3. **Review**: Pulseboard presents proposed actions for correction, rejection,
+   or confirmation.
+4. **Confirm**: the facilitator explicitly confirms text, owner, and due date.
+5. **Value realization**: the configured provider receives one reminder and
+   the facilitator sees its delivery status.
+6. **Follow-up**: the team can identify actions that are owned versus overdue
+   and unowned during the pilot review.
+
+## Functional Requirements
+
+### Core Features
+
+| Product promise | Planned delivery |
+|---|---|
+| PRM-001 | E001 transcript upload and proposed action extraction |
+| PRM-002 | E001 explicit confirmation gate for text, owner, and due date |
+| PRM-003 | E002 configured-provider reminder and delivery status |
+| PRM-004 | E001 workspace authorization and real-role negative probe |
+
+#### Feature Group 1: Reviewable action workflow
+
+**Transcript upload and proposal extraction**
+
+- **Description**: accept a workspace-scoped transcript and create proposed
+  action items from it.
+- **User stories**:
+  - As a facilitator, I want to upload a transcript so that likely action items
+    are collected for review.
+  - As a facilitator, I want to see proposals associated with my workspace so
+    that I do not see another team's meeting content.
+- **Acceptance criteria**:
+  - Uploading a transcript creates zero or more proposed actions in the same
+    workspace.
+  - A workspace member cannot read another workspace's transcripts or actions.
+- **Priority**: P0.
+
+**Explicit confirmation gate**
+
+- **Description**: a facilitator can edit and confirm proposal text, owner,
+  and due date; incomplete proposals cannot be scheduled or delivered.
+- **User stories**:
+  - As a facilitator, I want to correct a proposed action before it affects a
+    colleague.
+  - As a facilitator, I want confirmation to fail when an owner or due date is
+    missing so that no ambiguous reminder is sent.
+- **Acceptance criteria**:
+  - Confirmation records the reviewed text, owner, and due date.
+  - Delivery is unavailable until all three fields are explicitly confirmed.
+- **Priority**: P0.
+
+#### Feature Group 2: Configurable reminder delivery
+
+**Provider-backed single reminder and status**
+
+- **Description**: send exactly one reminder for a confirmed action through a
+  configured provider and expose its outcome.
+- **User stories**:
+  - As a facilitator, I want to see whether a reminder was delivered so that I
+    can follow up when delivery fails.
+- **Acceptance criteria**:
+  - The provider is selected through configuration rather than embedded in
+    confirmation logic.
+  - A confirmed action produces at most one delivery request unless an explicit
+    retry is later introduced and recorded.
+  - The UI exposes pending, delivered, or failed status.
+- **Priority**: P0.
+
+### Platform Requirements
+
+- **Web**: browser UI for desktop meeting-facilitation workflows; responsive
+  layout is expected but no mobile-native application is in scope.
+- **Mobile**: no native mobile app in the pilot.
+- **Desktop**: modern supported browsers; exact support matrix is an E000
+  delivery decision.
+
+### Integration Requirements
+
+| System | Type | Purpose | Priority |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Reminder provider (unselected) | Adapter/API | Deliver one confirmed reminder and return status | P0 |
+
+## Non-Functional Requirements
+
+### Performance
+
+- Typical upload/review interactions target under two seconds excluding
+  extraction or provider time that is explicitly surfaced to the facilitator.
+- Pilot scale is five teams; no high-throughput target is asserted without
+  evidence.
+
+### Reliability
+
+- Preserve delivery attempts and their statuses durably.
+- A provider failure must be visible and must not be reported as delivery.
+- E000 establishes backup, migration, and rollback practices for the pilot.
+
+### Security
+
+- Authentication is required for pilot users.
+- Authorization is workspace-membership based for every transcript/action read
+  and write.
+- The cross-workspace isolation claim requires a negative probe using the real
+  request role.
+- No regulated health or payment data is in scope; transcripts remain
+  confidential workspace data.
+
+### Usability
+
+- The confirmation gate must make the missing text, owner, or due date obvious.
+- The facilitator LARP must cover upload, review, confirmation, and delivery
+  status without relying on a hidden technical workflow.
+- The review flow should make first value available in one meeting follow-up.
+
+### Scalability
+
+- Start with a modular monolith and relational database.
+- Keep extraction and delivery behind interfaces so a later worker/service can
+  be introduced based on pilot evidence.
+
+## Design Principles
+
+### User Experience Principles
+
+1. **Human confirmation is the decision**: proposals are suggestions; a
+   facilitator's explicit confirmation authorizes delivery.
+2. **Show the operational truth**: status must distinguish pending, delivered,
+   and failed rather than imply success.
+3. **Workspace is a hard boundary**: the UI and API both scope work to the
+   active workspace.
+
+### Technical Principles
+
+1. **Enforce invariants at the API boundary**: UI affordances alone cannot
+   authorize delivery.
+2. **Persist observable transitions**: review and delivery states are durable
+   records that runtime evidence can inspect.
+3. **Defer provider selection safely**: provider-specific code cannot weaken
+   the confirmation invariant.
+
+## Constraints & Assumptions
+
+### Business Constraints
+
+- **Timeline**: four-week pilot.
+- **Resources**: two engineers.
+- **Pilot size**: five teams.
+- **Legal/data scope**: no regulated health or payment data.
+
+### Technical Constraints
+
+- A Python API and browser UI are required.
+- The reminder provider is not selected.
+- Non-goals are meeting recording, calendar replacement, and autonomous
+  outbound messaging.
+
+### Assumptions
+
+1. **Relational workspace-scoped storage**: PostgreSQL is a reversible pilot
+   choice; if unavailable, use an equivalent transactional relational store.
+2. **Authenticated pilot access**: the auth mechanism is intentionally deferred
+   to E000; if unavailable, the pilot cannot claim workspace isolation.
+3. **Single reminder semantics**: a delivery attempt is created only after
+   confirmation; retry behaviour is out of scope unless separately specified.
+
+## Release Strategy
+
+### MVP Scope
+
+The MVP is the complete transcript-to-confirmation-to-one-delivery path with
+workspace isolation and visible status. It deliberately excludes recording,
+calendar replacement, autonomous messaging, provider expansion, and advanced
+analytics.
+
+#### MVP Features
+
+- Infrastructure, test, deployment, and observability baseline.
+- Workspace-scoped transcript upload and action proposal review.
+- Explicit confirmation of text, owner, and due date.
+- Configured-provider delivery and recorded status.
+
+#### MVP Success Criteria
+
+- Runtime evidence exercises upload to confirmation to delivery.
+- Real-role negative probe denies cross-workspace access.
+- Facilitator LARP completes the workflow and judges it usable.
+- Pilot measures the stated review and unowned-overdue outcomes.
+
+### Release Phases
+
+**Phase 0: Development foundation**
+
+- Features: E000 testing, CI, environments, migration and observability base.
+- Success: feature work has a repeatable test/build/deploy path.
+
+**Phase 1: Reviewable action workflow**
+
+- Features: E001 workspace boundary, upload, proposals, and confirmation.
+- Success: a facilitator can create and explicitly confirm a complete action.
+
+**Phase 2: Reminder delivery pilot**
+
+- Features: E002 provider adapter, one delivery attempt, and status.
+- Success: the end-to-end evidence path is available to pilot teams.
+
+### Rollout Strategy
+
+- **Beta program**: onboard up to five teams after E002 validation.
+- **Feature flags**: optional provider configuration/release gating if the
+  selected deployment tooling supports it.
+- **Rollback plan**: roll back application releases; preserve data and mark
+  unsent/failed delivery states truthfully rather than re-sending automatically.
+
+## Success Metrics
+
+### Key Performance Indicators
+
+| Category | Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| User | Proposal review rate | 80% during pilot | Confirmed/rejected proposals divided by proposals created |
+| Outcome | Unowned overdue actions | 30% reduction in four weeks | Agreed pilot baseline versus pilot review |
+| Adoption | Teams using workflow | Five teams | Workspace activity records |
+| Technical | Cross-workspace authorization | 0 successful negative probes | Runtime authorization test evidence |
+| Technical | Delivery-state integrity | Every request has recorded status | Delivery-attempt records versus provider calls |
+
+### Measurement Plan
+
+- **Analytics**: record proposal creation, review, confirmation, provider
+  request, and delivery-result events with workspace-safe identifiers.
+- **Feedback loops**: facilitator feedback at onboarding and pilot close.
+- **Review cycle**: weekly during the four-week pilot.
+
+## Risk Analysis
+
+| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigation | Owner |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Extraction quality reduces trust | Medium | High | Editable proposals and mandatory confirmation | Product/engineering |
+| Tenant data exposure | Low | High | API-level membership enforcement and real-role negative probe | Engineering |
+| Provider selection delays delivery | Medium | Medium | Provider adapter; finalize provider inside E002 | Product/engineering |
+| Schedule leaves insufficient validation | Medium | High | E000 first; scope limited to two product epics | Engineering |
+
+## Dependencies
+
+### External Dependencies
+
+- **Reminder provider**: must be selected and configured before real E002
+  delivery validation.
+
+### Internal Dependencies
+
+- **E000**: must establish the test/build/deploy baseline before product epics.
+- **E001**: must provide confirmed workspace-scoped actions before E002 can
+  deliver reminders.
+
+## Appendices
+
+### A. Research Data
+
+None supplied or used.
+
+### B. Technical Architecture
+
+See `architecture.md`.
+
+### C. Mockups/Wireframes
+
+None supplied; UI states are specified at epic/story level.
+
+### D. Glossary
+
+- **Proposal**: an extracted candidate action item.
+- **Confirmed action**: a proposal whose text, owner, and due date a facilitator
+  explicitly confirmed.
+- **Delivery status**: the recorded outcome of the configured provider request.
+
+## Revision History
+
+| Version | Date | Changes | Author |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1.0.0 | 2026-08-11 | Initial canonical project plan | Codex |
