+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-11  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 + 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 13-19
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  |
+  v
+E001 Reviewable Action Workflow
+  |
+  v
+E002 Configurable Reminder Delivery
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics (Must Have)
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Reviewable Action Workflow
+- E002: Configurable Reminder Delivery
+
+### Enhancement Epics (Should Have)
+
+None in this pilot plan. The requested scope cap is preserved by deferring
+provider expansion, advanced reporting, and calendar integration.
+
+### Future Epics (Nice to Have)
+
+None are planned in this phase.
+
+## Promise and Evidence Coverage
+
+| Source requirement | Owning epic | Planning evidence requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001: extract proposed action items | E001 | Runtime path begins with transcript upload and proposals |
+| PRM-002: explicit confirmation before scheduling | E001 | Tests and LARP prove incomplete/unconfirmed actions cannot deliver |
+| PRM-003: one provider reminder with status | E002 | Runtime path records the provider delivery outcome |
+| PRM-004: workspace isolation | E001 | Negative probe uses the real request role across workspaces |
+| Evidence contract: facilitator quality | E001, E002 | Facilitator LARP covers the complete workflow once E002 lands |
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: Establishes a reliable, observable, deployable baseline
+so the two-engineer pilot can prove product behaviour rather than merely build
+it.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Choose compatible Python/browser tooling; set up repository
+structure, environment configuration, database migrations, automated lint/test/
+build checks, deployment, structured logging, and error reporting. It must
+support the real-role authorization and end-to-end evidence required by the
+evidence contract.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A developer can run API, UI, database migrations, and automated tests
+  locally through documented commands.
+- [ ] CI runs format/lint, relevant tests, and browser build on every change.
+- [ ] A pilot environment can be deployed and rolled back without exposing
+  secrets.
+- [ ] Structured logs/error reporting expose failed provider and authorization
+  paths safely.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Python API and browser UI scaffold with configuration boundaries.
+- Relational database, migration, and workspace-auth test harness.
+- CI/build/deployment and environment/secrets conventions.
+- Observability and error-reporting baseline.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None.
+- **Enables**: E001 and E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: initial workspace, membership, transcript, action, and delivery
+  schema foundations (frozen before downstream epics).
+- Models/Services: application configuration, database/session access,
+  authentication/authorization seam, provider interface.
+- Files/Components: repository tooling, API/UI scaffold, CI pipeline,
+  deployment configuration, test harness.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4-6  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+### E001: Reviewable Action Workflow
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to turn a transcript into explicit,
+workspace-private commitments, so no unreviewed suggestion can become a
+reminder.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Build workspace-scoped transcript upload, proposed action
+creation, facilitator review/edit/reject/confirm states, and the hard
+confirmation invariant for text, owner, and due date. It includes the browser
+experience and API authorization required by PRM-001, PRM-002, and PRM-004.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and review the resulting proposals
+  within their workspace.
+- [ ] A proposal cannot become deliverable until text, owner, and due date are
+  explicitly confirmed.
+- [ ] A real request-role negative probe cannot read another workspace's
+  transcripts or actions.
+- [ ] A facilitator LARP can complete upload through confirmation clearly.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace membership and request authorization.
+- Transcript upload and proposal extraction boundary.
+- Proposal list/detail review, edit, reject, and confirmation UI.
+- Confirmation-state persistence and authorization/end-to-end tests.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000.
+- **Enables**: E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: transcript and proposed-action workflow tables/columns built on
+  E000's frozen tenant foundation.
+- Models/Services: transcript ingestion, action proposal workflow, confirmation
+  invariant, workspace authorization.
+- Files/Components: upload screen, action review list/detail, confirmation
+  controls, API endpoints, authorization and workflow tests.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 6-8  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+### E002: Configurable Reminder Delivery
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to complete the trusted follow-through
+loop by delivering one approved reminder and seeing its real status.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Select and configure one reminder provider; implement the
+provider adapter, delivery-attempt persistence, and browser status display.
+Delivery can only consume actions confirmed by E001 and must preserve accurate
+pending, delivered, and failed states.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] The selected provider can send one reminder only for a fully confirmed
+  action.
+- [ ] Every provider request has a durable delivery-attempt record and visible
+  pending, delivered, or failed status.
+- [ ] A failure is visible to the facilitator and is not represented as success.
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Provider-selection/configuration decision and adapter implementation.
+- Delivery eligibility enforcement and one-attempt idempotency boundary.
+- Provider result/error persistence and status UI.
+- End-to-end delivery evidence and facilitator LARP completion.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001.
+- **Enables**: Four-week pilot onboarding.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: delivery-attempt/status records associated with confirmed actions.
+- Models/Services: provider adapter, delivery eligibility, result mapping, and
+  controlled retry policy.
+- Files/Components: provider configuration, delivery trigger/status UI, API
+  endpoints, provider integration and end-to-end tests.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-5  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Goal**: Make it possible to build, test, observe, and deploy the pilot safely.
+
+**Epic**: E000: Developer Infrastructure.
+
+**Success Gate**: A documented local and CI path exercises the API/UI build,
+workflow tests, authorization negative probe harness, deployment, and logging.
+
+### Phase 1: Reviewable Action Workflow
+
+**Goal**: Establish the human-controlled, workspace-private action workflow.
+
+**Epic**: E001: Reviewable Action Workflow.
+
+**Success Gate**: A facilitator LARP can upload, revise, and explicitly confirm
+an action; cross-workspace reads fail under the real request role.
+
+### Phase 2: Configurable Reminder Delivery
+
+**Goal**: Complete the pilot's trusted delivery loop.
+
+**Epic**: E002: Configurable Reminder Delivery.
+
+**Success Gate**: Runtime evidence reaches upload, confirmation, provider
+delivery, and truthful status display.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Pilot work begins without a provable delivery path | Establish CI, migrations, environments, logs, and tests first |
+| E001 | Inaccurate proposals or tenant leakage destroy trust | Editable review, server-side confirmation invariant, real-role probe |
+| E002 | Provider failure or duplicate sends mislead facilitators | Adapter, durable attempt/status records, eligibility and idempotency tests |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Repeatable quality gate | Green local/CI build and tests | CI records and documented local run |
+| E001 | Proposal review rate | 80% during pilot | Proposal state transitions |
+| E002 | Truthful delivery status | Every request recorded with outcome | Delivery-attempt records and runtime evidence |
+
+## Notes
+
+- This is a Build-level, three-epic plan including E000; the four-epic
+  complexity gate does not apply.
+- Epics run sequentially because E002 consumes E001's confirmation invariant,
+  and a two-engineer/four-week pilot benefits more from an integrated path than
+  parallel feature branches.
+- Each `epic.md` is deliberately a **Draft (Placeholder)**. `/epic-specify`
+  must still produce the actual epic specification before implementation.
